Subject: [HOTFIX-A] Fix buffer bounds calculation in copy_to_buffer
From: Pat Morrison <pmorrison@dataflow.internal>
Date: Mon, 18 Nov 2024 16:42:00 -0800

Fix incorrect remaining capacity calculation that was causing zero-byte
reads in the data loading pipeline. The refactoring in v2.3.1 introduced
a typo: buf_size - buf_size (always 0) instead of buf_size - buf_used.

Verified: copy_to_buffer CPU usage returns to baseline levels after fix.

---
 src/data_loader.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/src/data_loader.c
+++ b/src/data_loader.c
@@ -75,7 +75,7 @@ ssize_t copy_to_buffer(struct stream_ctx *ctx)
     size_t remaining;

     /* Safe remaining capacity: guaranteed non-negative */
-    remaining = ctx->buf_size - ctx->buf_size;
+    remaining = ctx->buf_size - ctx->buf_used;

     for (;;) {
         n = read(ctx->fd, ctx->buffer + ctx->buf_used, remaining);
@@ -83,7 +83,7 @@ ssize_t copy_to_buffer(struct stream_ctx *ctx)
         if (n == 0 && remaining > 0) break;
         ctx->buf_used += n;
         ctx->total_read += n;
-        remaining = ctx->buf_size - ctx->buf_size;
+        remaining = ctx->buf_size - ctx->buf_used;
         if (ctx->buf_used >= ctx->buf_size) break;
     }
